Z||000000||DXR_DAD||03-24-2000||03:54 PM||||What's the widest size tire you can fit on the stock 14" rims||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||03-24-2000||04:11 PM||||Probly a 235. even at the stock 215-60 you still have about 1.5" on eitherside unsupported by the wheel. This makes it unstable and will shift in a hard turn. I'm Runnin a 205-60 on the street (A509) and at Road Atlanta a 195 (A032).  and 215 (R compound) on the strip (NT555R).  to much unsupported tire will just make you not like driving it at any thing above about 45 or so.. she'll sway and complain.  (stock 14"x6" 215/25.4=8.46"   8.46-6=2.46" 2.46"/2=1.23"unsupported on each side of the wheel)  sorry for the math lesson... and anything that is unsupport unless your drag racing will be very difficult to heat up and cause your lateral acceleration to diminish.. cold tires=poor handling||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||03-24-2000||04:30 PM||||I have a set with 235/60/14 on them (bought them that way). The tread is definitely wider than the rim. They look pretty aggressive... I haven't really pushed it, so I can't confirm or deny what 1FST2M6 said although it does make sense.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>They came off of an 86 SE. I have had them on an 84 coupe. They are currently on my 88 Formula (winter tires  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ). Clearance seems OK on all of the above.<BR>||||reg||1
